==Description==
'''PVP Intermission Lobby''' is the main hub for [[PVP]] mode matches. It contains four panels with a random map in them, an inventory area that allows the player to access the inventory, though with some sections like crates disabled and a super computer that allows the player to override the current maps if they are a VIP and the match is not a ranked match.

On top of the interactable spots on the map, there are three buttons on the screen. These are veto, which if the specified number of players votes for overrides every currently selected map, ready, which instantly starts the match and inventory, which opens the inventory.

Entering the '''PVP Intermission Lobby''' through private servers gives the player access to unlimited map overrides without VIP, allows them to play on community maps and gives them unlimited vetos. However, it also adds in a 25 second timer whenever a map is overridden or all maps are vetoed.

==Appearance==
The '''PVP Intermission Lobby''' is a small island made entirely out of stone. The island appears to be some sort of battlefield, as it has multiple barricades, a statue with a hole in its chest and another statue wielding a sword.

There is a small armory which contains various weapons, crates and barrels. Four panels can be seen which display a map and their difficulty. Next to these panels, there is a super computer.

